A \emph{feedforward \ac{relu} network} of depth $L\in\NN$ has \emph{layer widths} $d^{(0)},\ldots,d^{(L)}\in\NN$, weights $\Wl{l}\in\RR^{d^{(l)}\times d^{(l-1)}}$, and biases $b^{(l)}\in\RR^{d^{(l)}}$. For input $\actl{0}=x\in\RR^{d^{(0)}}$, its \emph{pre-activations} $\preactl{l}$, \emph{activations} $\actl{l}$, and function $f:\RR^{d^{(0)}}\to\RR^{d^{(L)}}$ satisfy
\begin{align}
	\preactl{l} &\coloneqq \Wl{l}\actl{l-1}+b^{(l)}, && l=1,\ldots,L, \label{eq:forward_recursion}\\
	\actl{l} &\coloneqq \relu\bigl(\preactl{l}\bigr), && l=1,\ldots,L-1, \notag\\
	f(x) &= \actl{L}\coloneqq\preactl{L}. \label{eq:network_function}
\end{align}
Here $\relu(z)=\max\{z,0\}$ acts componentwise on the hidden layers $1,\ldots,L-1$; the output is affine. We use $\relu'(0)=0$, so gates $\1\{\preactl{l}_i>0\}$ are closed at zero.

